# =============================================================================
# deploy/.env.compose — Compose-level settings (template)
# =============================================================================
# Copy to .env.compose beside this file on the VM. It is read by
# `docker compose --env-file` for substitution in compose.yaml.
#
# There is no app.env counterpart, unlike the ResidentOps lane this is modelled
# on, and there is nothing missing. The hosted addon has no secrets: no model
# key, no database, no channel credentials, no install secret. Every per-user
# setting lives in that user's own install URL. If a future change introduces a
# secret here, that is the moment to add an app.env and an `env_file:` — do not
# put one in this file, which is substituted into labels and can end up in
# `docker inspect`.
#
# .env.compose is gitignored. Never commit a filled-in copy. CI can supply the
# whole file through the optional COMPOSE_ENV secret.
# =============================================================================

# --- Image -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pushed by .github/workflows/deploy.yml. Lowercase, no tag here.
SOFF_IMAGE=ghcr.io/<owner>/stremio-offline
# Pin to a commit SHA for a reproducible deploy; use a previous SHA to roll back.
SOFF_IMAGE_TAG=latest

# --- Shared Traefik edge -----------------------------------------------------
# Must match the network the Synpse/Traefik stack created. This stack never binds
# host ports 80/443.
TRAEFIK_NETWORK=synapse-edge

# The Traefik router rule. Backticks are required by Traefik.
#
# soffline.synpse.app is under *.synpse.app, so the Synpse stack's existing
# wildcard Cloudflare Origin Cert already covers it and NO new certificate work
# is needed. Any other zone would need its own cert added to the Synpse stack's
# deploy/certs + deploy/tls.yml first, and Cloudflare SSL/TLS mode Full (strict).
SOFF_HOST_RULE=Host(`soffline.synpse.app`)

# Hostname used by the edge health gate in deploy.sh. One host, no backticks — it
# is sent as a Host: header.
SOFF_PRIMARY_DOMAIN=soffline.synpse.app

# --- Optional overrides ------------------------------------------------------
# Router priority. 110 puts this router above BOTH Synpse routers, which matters
# if SYNAPSE_HOST_RULE ever carries the `HostRegexp(.+\.synpse\.app)` default
# from traefik-edge.md — that regexp matches our host too. Raising it is safe
# because our own rule matches only soffline.synpse.app. See the long comment in
# compose.yaml before changing it.
# SOFF_ROUTER_PRIORITY=110
#
# Per client IP per minute, applied by Traefik before anything reaches the addon.
# This bounds how hard this host can be made to hammer users' upstream addons.
# SOFF_RATE=120
# SOFF_RATE_BURST=240
#
# SOFF_COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=soffline
